00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Shark Tale is a 2004 American animated adventure film directed by Vicky Jenson, Bibo Bergeron, and Rob
Letterman (in his feature length directorial debut), and written by Letterman and Michael J.

13
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
Produced by DreamWorks Animation, the film features the voices of Will Smith, Robert De
Niro, Renée Zellweger, Angelina Jolie, Jack Black, and Martin Scorsese.

14
00:57:16,363 --> 00:57:22,363
It follows an underachieving fish named Oscar (Smith) who falsely claims to have killed the son of a
shark mob boss Don Lino (De Niro) in an attempt to advance his community standing.

15
01:01:21,818 --> 01:01:27,818
Oscar teams up with the mobster's younger son
Lenny (Black) to keep up the facade.

16
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Shark Tale premiered at the Venice Film Festival on September 10, 2004, and
was theatrically released in the United States on October 1.

17
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
It made $374.6 million worldwide against its $75 million budget, finishing
its theatrical run as the ninth-highest-grossing film of 2004.

18
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
The film received mixed reviews from critics; advocacy groups criticized
the film for its use of Italian-American stereotypes.

19
01:17:43,636 --> 01:17:49,636
It was nominated for Best Animated Feature at the 77th Academy Awards.

20
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
The film explores themes of fish, secret love,
hero, mission of murder, vegetarian.

